# Generated artifacts.
#
# NOTE: data/doc_embeddings.npy is deliberately NOT ignored — it is committed.
# Streamlit Community Cloud starts from a fresh container with no cache, and
# encoding the 14,955-chunk corpus there costs ~285 s and ~308 MB of transient
# memory, which blows both the boot timeout and the ~1 GB container limit.
# Shipping the 23 MB matrix turns a 308 s boot into a 23 s boot. It is safe to
# commit because stage 04 validates it against a SHA-256 content fingerprint and
# silently re-encodes if the corpus or model ever changes.
#
# faiss.index IS ignored: it is rebuilt from the committed vectors in ~0.05 s,
# so committing it would add 23 MB for no benefit.
data/faiss.index

